  - machine learning
  - molecular property prediction
  - database
abstract: >
  NIST-OrgThermo-ML is a curated database of standard enthalpies of formation
  (ΔfH° at 298.15 K, 1 bar) for 11,860 unique organic molecules. It combines
  166 experimental gas-phase values from the NIST Chemistry WebBook (NIST SRD 69)
  with 11,637 computational values derived from the QM9 dataset (B3LYP/6-31G(2df,p)
  level of theory) via a thermochemical cycle using literature atomic reference
  energies at the same DFT level. The database includes 302 total experimental
  observations (gas/liquid/solid), 12,000 computational observations, a structure
  registry with InChIKey/SMILES/CAS identifiers, and an ML-ready dataset with
  RDKit descriptors and formula features. QM9 vs experimental validation on 88
  matched molecules yields MAE = 80.12 kJ/mol, RMSE = 87.83 kJ/mol, R² = 0.9624.
